        "id": 236369,
        "name": "Rabit",
        "username": "Rabit",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/{size}/7330_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-27T13:34:18.954Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I think catDreaming is getting it from this line, <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/takewalker\">@TakeWalker</a>:</p>\n<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Ability Text\" data-post=\"1\" data-topic=\"28341\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Ability Text:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Each time you use a Reaction after the first one <em>each turn</em>,</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I honestly hadn’t caught this bit, always reading it as paying the cost after using the first for the <em>round</em>. (Basically I was interpreting the italicized text in the quote above as “each round” instead of “each turn”.) But catDreaming’s point is a good one, and makes me wonder if this was a typo (and meant to be “each round”) or if it works the way catDreaming has laid out.</p>",
