      {
        "id": 236372,
        "name": "",
        "username": "fjur",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/fjur/{size}/4849_2.png",
        "created_at": "2021-03-27T14:54:39.044Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I agree with <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/takewalker\">@TakeWalker</a> and <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/rabit\">@Rabit</a>’s readings of the Ability. I, too, thought it read “once per round,” for the longest time. Perhaps it is a typo (and someone should bring that to the attention of the appropriate persons), but until proven wrong, I think we should interpret its wording exactly.</p>\n<p>As for <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/catdreaming\">@catDreaming</a>’s interpretations of the Ability’s benefits:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I agree with this first point’s effect, although I think I would rephrase it is, “You may use 1 Reaction per turn, instead of per round, for free.”</li>\n<li>I would argue that the damage-or-twist happens after the extra Reaction, because the Ability reads, “Each time,” which to me implies a triggered action, and an action cannot happen before its trigger. Plus, it lets a Hero make a Noble Heroic Sacrifice.</li>\n</ul>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-03-27T14:54:39.044Z",
